@startuml ESP Device Activation Mechanism
title ESP Device Activation and Flashing Process

note over Script, ESP
  **Technologies Used:**
  • esptool.py - ESP32 flashing tool
  • espressif/idf - Official ESP-IDF Docker container
  • mklittlefs - LittleFS filesystem builder
  • LittleFS/SPIFFS - Embedded filesystem
  • Docker - Containerization platform
end note

participant "flash_device.sh\nScript" as Script
participant "espressif/idf\nContainer" as IDF
participant "ESP Device\n(via USB)" as ESP
participant "python-prepare-esp\nContainer" as Prepare
participant "API Backend" as API
participant "Database" as DB
participant "mklittlefs\nContainer" as LittleFS

== Step 1: Read MAC Address ==
Script -> IDF: Launch espressif/idf container
IDF -> ESP: Execute esptool.py read_mac
ESP -> IDF: Return physical MAC address
IDF -> Script: MAC address
Script -> Script: Store MAC for registration

== Step 2: Generate Device Credentials ==
Script -> Script: Generate random device secret (128-bit)
Script -> Script: Create config files:\n• device_id.txt (MAC)\n• device_secret.txt (secret)\n• ca.crt (CA certificate)

== Step 3: Register Device in Backend ==
Script -> Prepare: Launch python-prepare-esp container
Prepare -> API: POST /admin/esp/create\n{mac, secret}
API -> API: Validate admin token
API -> DB: Create ESP device record\n(MAC, secret)
DB -> API: Device created
API -> DB: Create default sensors/actuators
DB -> API: Devices provisioned
API -> Prepare: Success response
Prepare -> Script: Registration complete

== Step 4: Build LittleFS Filesystem ==
Script -> LittleFS: Launch mklittlefs container
LittleFS -> LittleFS: Create LittleFS image from:\n• device_id.txt\n• device_secret.txt\n• ca.crt
LittleFS -> Script: littlefs.bin ready

== Step 5: Erase ESP Flash ==
Script -> IDF: Execute esptool.py erase_flash
IDF -> ESP: Erase entire flash memory
ESP -> IDF: Flash erased
IDF -> Script: Erase complete

== Step 6: Flash Complete Firmware ==
Script -> IDF: Flash bootloader (0x1000)
IDF -> ESP: Write bootloader.bin
Script -> IDF: Flash partition table (0x8000)
IDF -> ESP: Write partition-table.bin
Script -> IDF: Flash OTA data
IDF -> ESP: Write ota_data_initial.bin
Script -> IDF: Flash application
IDF -> ESP: Write app.bin
Script -> IDF: Flash LittleFS filesystem
IDF -> ESP: Write littlefs.bin
IDF -> Script: All flashing complete

== Step 7: Device Ready ==
ESP -> ESP: Restart with new firmware
ESP -> ESP: Load configuration from LittleFS:\n• MAC address\n• Device secret\n• CA certificate
ESP -> ESP: Device ready for Bluetooth pairing
ESP -> ESP: Can authenticate to backend
ESP -> ESP: Ready to work in ecosystem

@enduml